# The literals of an owner's installed contract files that this fork's modules still write, which
# tools/restated_declarations.py finds: <module> <literal> <sites> issue=<owner>/<repo>#<n>. It only gets shorter: a literal
# read from its owner leaves its line, and the line goes in the same change (Open-Mixer/zynthian-ui#4). Each line names
# the owner's issue that removes it (a per-site allowance, see the tool's header); sites are counted per module and literal.
# Not here: the name argument of a call into the owner's library (ruling D22), and a host's id (the VERB_HOSTS table).

# the four refusals the chain manager treats as transient: a table of codes, which the owner is to publish as a class
zyngine/zynthian_chain_manager.py reply.plugin-hostd.gave-up 1 issue=Open-Mixer/plugin-hostd-protocol#23
zyngine/zynthian_chain_manager.py reply.plugin-hostd.pin-refused 1 issue=Open-Mixer/plugin-hostd-protocol#23
zyngine/zynthian_chain_manager.py reply.plugin-hostd.verb-dropped 1 issue=Open-Mixer/plugin-hostd-protocol#23
zyngine/zynthian_chain_manager.py reply.plugin-hostd.worker-spawn 1 issue=Open-Mixer/plugin-hostd-protocol#23

